From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:00:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 265/342] usb_hid: leave the AB13X headset adapter's phantom
 buttons alone

The adapter (001f:0b21) declares ten media buttons, has none, and reports
"play" going up and down by itself every few seconds. Each event reset the
screen saver's idle time. Tested on the board that has it: no events, and the
screen saver starts. Its audio is usb_audio's, which this doesn't touch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/usb_hid/Driver.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/usb_hid/Driver.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/usb_hid/Driver.cpp
index 6d1445da49..82a61dbd69 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/usb_hid/Driver.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/usb_hid/Driver.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,12 @@ usb_support_descriptor gBlackListedDevices[] = {
 	{
 		// wacom devices are handled by the dedicated wacom driver
 		0, 0, 0, USB_VENDOR_WACOM, 0
+	},
+	{
+		// AB13X USB-C headset adapter: declares ten media buttons, has none,
+		// and reports "play" going up and down by itself every few seconds,
+		// which counts as input (no screen saver). Its audio is usb_audio's.
+		0, 0, 0, 0x001f, 0x0b21
 	}
 
 };
